Every charge of a request still open counts an overrun, not only the one that reaches its end.
A thread charged twice within one request, as at a bind or a wait's span, would count overruns it never ran.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place counted overruns otherwise than as a charge reached a request's end
Witness: fuzz lend-chain-of-two

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@ static uint64_t turn_vtime(const struct core *core, const struct place *p, uint6
         return p->vt;
     }
     uint64_t cost = units_divide((now - core->turn_from) * TIME_UNITS + units - 1, units);
-    if (room != 0 && cost >= room) {
+    if (room != 0) {
         own->overruns++;
     }
     return cost < bound - p->vt ? p->vt + cost : bound;
